  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full-length set at The Majestic Theatre in Madison, Wisconsin, on Tuesday, May 14, 2019 [1]. The recording, captured and transferred by Liz Hamilton, runs for 99 minutes and includes twenty songs [1]. This performance is the 278th in the archive’s collection for the band, following a show at Mr. Smalls Theatre on May 8, 2019 [2]. The setlist opens with “Clemency for the Wizard King” and “Younger,” both from the album *In League with Dragons* [1]. It continues with “The Coroner’s Gambit” and “Moon Over Goldsboro,” the latter from *Get Lonely* [1]. The band plays “In League with Dragons” and “Sax Rohmer #1,” the latter from *Heretic Pride* [1]. “Wear Black” from *Goths* is also included [1]. A notable moment occurs with “Whole Wide World,” which is the first appearance of the song in 27 archived shows, a gap of 526 days [2]. The set proceeds with “Alpha Omega” and “Waylon Jennings Live!” [1]. “Passaic, 1975” and “Cotton” from *We Shall All Be Healed* follow [1]. “San Bernardino” from *Heretic Pride* and “Cadaver Sniffing Dog” from *In League with Dragons* are played next [1]. “Insurance Fraud #2” from *The Coroner’s Gambit* is a rare track, with only five archived performances [2]. “Sicilian Crest” from *In League with Dragons* closes the main set [1]. The encore features “Possum By Night,” “See America Right,” “Heel Turn 2,” and “No Children” [1]. This is the only available recording of the event [1].",
